//is cloud computing the best choice ??
   Cloud computing is extremely useful, but it’s not the best choice in all cases. Depending on factors like security, latency, cost, or legacy systems, alternatives like edge computing, client-server, or on-premise infrastructure might be more optimal.
    | Model                       | Use When                                                                                        |
    | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
    | **Client-Server Computing** | You need centralized control and data, like in small enterprises or internal tools.             |
    | **Centralized Computing**   | Simple applications that don’t need scaling or distributed access.                              |
    | **Edge Computing**          | Real-time decision-making near data source (e.g., autonomous cars, smart factories).            |
    | **Grid Computing**          | When breaking large tasks into small ones across multiple machines (e.g., scientific research). |


